      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-78866 has center (-1,-4) directly from its translated squares. Completing squares gives 3(x-3)^2-2(y-2)^2=6 for q-78872 and (y+4)^2-3(x+4)^2=9 for q-116122, establishing their centers. For q-76108, f^{-1}(5)=2 and f'(2)=4 ln(2), so the inverse derivative is its reciprocal. In q-77452, the diagram shows a displacement of five grid units right and six down; a and b each span two units, giving coefficients 2.5 and 3. For q-120304, OJ=h+(5/8)(i-h)=(3/8)h+(5/8)i. For q-36314, A^2=3I and A^4=9I. For q-130688, K^2 has rows (7,4) and (12,7), so K^2-4K+I=0. Direct complex matrix multiplication verifies all four entries for q-39021. Taking entrywise imaginary coefficients gives q-76207. For q-106714, f(x) cannot equal 2, and every other real value is attained at x=1-3/(y-2). For q-113501, the excluded denominator root satisfies -2k/5=2/5, hence k=-1. For q-70641, x=-1, y=1+2t and z=-t give (y-1)/2=-z. For q-127519, Q-P=(-3,0,3), giving the stated symmetric equation with y=-3. The squared matrices in q-78534 and q-130616 are zero, so both sixth powers are zero. The source's temporary expressions involving division by zero in the line questions are explicitly identified as invalid and replaced by correct constant-coordinate equations.",
